{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor recognized the BI-RADS 4B priority, worked through information gaps with targeted questions and workspace queries, delivered a risk-stratified plan that correctly layered other nodules, addressed perioperative safety including hepatitis B and coagulation, provided red flags, and obtained teach-back. No serious or minor responsibility-chain error is present; all seven RC items are met. The trajectory demonstrates three completed high-order points (HO1, HO2, HO4) with independent evidence of repairing execution confusion, converting screenshot gaps into concrete instructions, and bounding residual uncertainty at closure. HO3 is partially triggered but not fully completed because reprioritization from post-surgical symptoms was not systemically re-sorted. No important non-chain defect blocks Strong. Grade 4 is warranted with one complete HO, exceeding the Strong threshold.",
